Definitions {#definitions}
==========================

A <dfn export>widget</dfn> is a thing that can be <dfn>frobnicated</dfn>.
Every [=widget=] has a <dfn for=widget>frob count</dfn>, initially 0.

<div algorithm>
    To <dfn>frobnicate</dfn> a [=widget=] |widget| by an integer |n|:

    1. Let |count| be |widget|'s [=widget/frob count=].
    1. Set |widget|'s [=widget/frob count=] to |count| + |n|.
    1. Return |count|.
</div>

The [=frobnicate=] algorithm is used by {{Widget/frobnicate()}}.

<wpt>
    anchors/anchor-position-001.html
</wpt>

IDL {#idl}
==========

<pre class=idl>
[Exposed=Window]
interface Widget {
    constructor();
    undefined frobnicate(long n);
    readonly attribute long frobCount;
};
</pre>

The <dfn method for=Widget>frobnicate(|n|)</dfn> method steps are to
[=frobnicate=] [=this=] by |n|.

The <dfn attribute for=Widget>frobCount</dfn> getter steps are to return
[=this=]'s [=widget/frob count=].

CSS {#css}
==========

<pre class=propdef>
Name: frob-color
Value: <<color>> | auto
Initial: auto
Applies to: all elements
Inherited: yes
Percentages: n/a
Computed value: as specified
Canonical order: per grammar
Animation type: by computed value
</pre>

The 'frob-color' property sets the color of a [=widget=].

<pre class=railroad>
T: frob(
N: <integer>
Opt:
    T: ,
    N: <color>
T: )
</pre>

